     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose is above the maximum.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg/day**, and for extended-release it's **2000 mg/day**. This order is double the immediate-release maximum. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI side effects with no added benefit to blood sugar control.\n\n**Common regimens that may be what you meant:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n- **1700 mg/day total, split as 850 mg twice daily** with meals\n- **1000 mg by mouth twice daily** with meals (2000 mg/day, a common target dose)\n\nIf the patient isn't already on metformin, the usual start is 500 mg once or twice daily (or 850 mg once daily), increased slowly so it's better tolerated.\n\nWhich regimen do you want? Or, if you do mean 1700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it to the order note."
      }
     ],
